# Update package READMEs

When changing structure or documented behavior in `gt-frontend` or `gt-backend`, update that package’s `README.md` in the same task.

## When to update

- New, removed, or renamed pages, stores, routes, models, middleware, or folders
- Auth / users / feature behavior that Feature notes describe
- Env vars, scripts, or conventions sections that become wrong

## What to keep accurate

- Project structure tree
- Routes / page ↔ store map (frontend) or layer conventions (backend)
- Feature notes

Do not leave README stale after structural or feature work. If nothing documented changed, skip the README edit.
